    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` build passed (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` DTO fields.\n\n**How it works now:** the memberId is `region` + two-digit fiscal year + the 8 upper-hex SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName` + a Luhn check digit over `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Example from the run: `NSW` + `27` + `16E6609E` + `1` = `NSW2716E6609E1`.\n\n**Structural-impact-minimizing choices:**\n- Reused the existing `customer_code` column as internal storage for the memberId, so I left the large `Owner` entity, `schema.sql`, `data.sql`, and the `.POST.yml` pipeline wiring **untouched**.\n- Collision handling (`DeduplicateCustomerCode`) and the check-digit helper (`CustomerCodeCheckDigit`) needed **no changes** \u2014 dedup already operates on the stored value, which is now the memberId, so collision handling applies to it automatically.\n- Every function I changed is a small method in a small class (`AssignCustomerCode`, `OwnerLocality.region`, the mapper interface method, `AuditOwnerCreated.service`, `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent.service`), keeping WMC_other and per-method complexity low.\n\n**Six files touched:**\n1. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 builds the full memberId (region + FY + hash8 + check digit).\n2. `OwnerLocality.region` \u2014 derives the region from the memberId's leading letter-run (no `-` split), so owner segment and locality still resolve.\n3. `OwnerMapper` \u2014 dropped `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings, added `memberId`.\n4. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 logs `memberId` (removed the membershipNumber helper).\n5. `EmitOwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 emits `memberId` in the structured event.\n6. `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed the three fields, added the `memberId` schema.\n\nThe fiscal-year value is embedded in the memberId via the shared `FiscalYear`, and the audit record and owner segment now reference the memberId.",
